[
  {
    "unit": 44,
    "page": 88,
    "width": 1488,
    "height": 2061,
    "title": "A / an and one",
    "lines": [
      {
        "width": 6.310025081839614,
        "height": 2.0105696788236593,
        "y": 2.0832873284527653,
        "text": "Unit",
        "x": 2.3756779361880342
      },
      {
        "width": 5.835010159400202,
        "height": 2.7616278854651344,
        "y": 4.505813946984006,
        "text": "44",
        "x": 2.414486878297887
      },
      {
        "width": 22.535211296491724,
        "height": 2.3326303054705955,
        "y": 4.94186046552324,
        "text": "A / an and one",
        "x": 13.279678110305449
      },
      {
        "width": 59.758549351846014,
        "height": 1.463638799613709,
        "y": 9.011627909799735,
        "text": "We use a before nouns and noun phrases that begin with a consonant sound.",
        "x": 13.279679034059107
      },
      {
        "width": 13.68209264611685,
        "height": 1.1728001380868602,
        "y": 9.156976755136537,
        "text": "Reminder → 16-7",
        "x": 78.06841040732387
      },
      {
        "width": 54.52716376191826,
        "height": 1.4653305771510472,
        "y": 10.755813956431226,
        "text": "If the noun or noun phrase starts with a vowel letter but begins with a",
        "x": 12.877263179049356
      },
      {
        "width": 24.94969726890646,
        "height": 1.3215324927255079,
        "y": 12.499999994447663,
        "text": "consonant sound, we also use a:",
        "x": 13.27967852450049
      },
      {
        "width": 19.517102805517055,
        "height": 1.6140628855397243,
        "y": 14.098837253166185,
        "text": "a university (/ə juːn .../)",
        "x": 16.29778662062769
      },
      {
        "width": 48.692153602518054,
        "height": 1.6140628855397243,
        "y": 14.098837254129137,
        "text": "a European (/ə jʊər .../)     a one-parent family (/ə wʌn .../)",
        "x": 38.028168661955036
      },
      {
        "width": 64.19627692109795,
        "height": 1.7264294924953405,
        "y": 16.417706052130075,
        "text": "We use an before words that begin with a vowel sound, including a silent letter 'h':",
        "x": 13.073147848456882
      },
      {
        "width": 9.267304533271375,
        "height": 1.2125092496233725,
        "y": 18.434443025006065,
        "text": "an orange",
        "x": 18.907595208197925
      },
      {
        "width": 9.8591548140331,
        "height": 1.0361919810075837,
        "y": 18.313953501114334,
        "text": "an Italian",
        "x": 29.17505035757098
      },
      {
        "width": 32.60982472409484,
        "height": 1.2967091642688722,
        "y": 18.187616006411677,
        "text": "an umbrella an hour an honour",
        "x": 41.84475854768503
      },
      {
        "width": 70.22132463352655,
        "height": 1.6197019589976436,
        "y": 19.912790742611584,
        "text": "and abbreviations said as individual letters that begin with A, E, F, H, I, L, M, N, O, R, S or X:",
        "x": 13.07847248232801
      },
      {
        "width": 18.108650945848037,
        "height": 1.621252720386046,
        "y": 21.511627950374645,
        "text": "an MP (/ən em piː/)",
        "x": 18.712274118848843
      },
      {
        "width": 26.994926698746223,
        "height": 1.7611426826129262,
        "y": 21.4313300343561,
        "text": "an FBI agent (/ən ef biː aɪ .../)",
        "x": 36.60315413640603
      },
      {
        "width": 21.931588777931786,
        "height": 1.4757629509231096,
        "y": 21.511627909067954,
        "text": "an IOU (/ən aɪ əʊ juː/)",
        "x": 63.78269655340709
      },
      {
        "width": 32.19315928797568,
        "height": 1.3081395198255907,
        "y": 24.12790698384294,
        "text": "But compare abbreviations said as words:",
        "x": 13.279677890826308
      },
      {
        "width": 70.22132463352655,
        "height": 1.6225215419765515,
        "y": 25.557710970392012,
        "text": "a NATO general (/ə neɪtəʊ .../) a FIFA official (/ə fiːfə .../) but an OPEC meeting (/ən",
        "x": 18.913482556581272
      },
      {
        "width": 9.665724026259554,
        "height": 1.4805791912208432,
        "y": 27.45738482009179,
        "text": "əʊpek .../)",
        "x": 19.513214443997462
      },
      {
        "width": 14.330535806635378,
        "height": 1.409734417002373,
        "y": 29.13765876474398,
        "text": "Note that we say:",
        "x": 13.0549980793262
      },
      {
        "width": 41.469889815135666,
        "height": 1.8552932776257802,
        "y": 30.60687003300011,
        "text": "• a history (book) but an (or a) historical (novel)",
        "x": 16.288446806027295
      },
      {
        "width": 69.01408369823167,
        "height": 1.6144857952365865,
        "y": 33.850630437882664,
        "text": "We use a / an (not one) to talk about a particular but unspecified person, thing or event:",
        "x": 12.87726399888479
      },
      {
        "width": 1.6096579131259712,
        "height": 1.3081395198255907,
        "y": 34.156976740813946,
        "text": "B",
        "x": 8.853118719493354
      },
      {
        "width": 25.15090614236811,
        "height": 1.467445218135266,
        "y": 35.596508266090154,
        "text": "• I really need a cup of coffee.",
        "x": 16.700200844589066
      },
      {
        "width": 48.289739957419776,
        "height": 1.6112433025607942,
        "y": 37.196896185838014,
        "text": "• You never see a police officer in this part of town, do you?",
        "x": 16.498993219495738
      },
      {
        "width": 56.53923608923471,
        "height": 1.463497829714755,
        "y": 39.670223096592274,
        "text": "We also use a / an, not one, in number and quantity expressions such as:",
        "x": 13.480884977650872
      },
      {
        "width": 17.553809381300407,
        "height": 1.517206066216692,
        "y": 41.42457570703942,
        "text": "• three times a year",
        "x": 16.670101868406363
      },
      {
        "width": 54.75556978615382,
        "height": 1.93116477574109,
        "y": 41.05864597367051,
        "text": "half an hour   a quarter of an hour   a day or so (= ‘about a day’)",
        "x": 34.9986318342542
      },
      {
        "width": 53.923539192445816,
        "height": 1.751093952315863,
        "y": 42.870999008265564,
        "text": "50 cents a (= each) litre (note we can also say '50 cents for one litre')",
        "x": 19.517103864541667
      },
      {
        "width": 68.04893247542843,
        "height": 2.3801178289315272,
        "y": 44.18614458367589,
        "text": "a week or two (= ‘between one and two weeks’; note we can also say ‘one or two weeks’)",
        "x": 19.698359111878236
      },
      {
        "width": 12.87726330500777,
        "height": 1.1661741828363437,
        "y": 46.50824440856539,
        "text": "a few a little",
        "x": 19.71830998512678
      },
      {
        "width": 18.108650945848037,
        "height": 1.3115230286502966,
        "y": 46.508244404626154,
        "text": "a huge number of ...",
        "x": 33.1991956450743
      },
      {
        "width": 56.941649734333,
        "height": 1.4548981571290032,
        "y": 48.83608145311155,
        "text": "We use a rather than one in the pattern a ... of ... with possessives, as in:",
        "x": 13.480885402181547
      },
      {
        "width": 23.74245428269909,
        "height": 1.6009518524377153,
        "y": 50.58139539314266,
        "text": "• She's a colleague of mine.",
        "x": 16.498994174152163
      },
      {
        "width": 24.181794607511133,
        "height": 1.6419049030825583,
        "y": 52.14513255159444,
        "text": "• That's a friend of Gabriel's.",
        "x": 16.88425704566262
      },
      {
        "width": 56.16005107920656,
        "height": 1.751735531855969,
        "y": 55.28844164308288,
        "text": "Before a singular countable noun one and a / an both refer to one thing:",
        "x": 13.469991399599532
      },
      {
        "width": 38.24417360367314,
        "height": 1.5988040964772243,
        "y": 57.11878032375659,
        "text": "We'll be in Australia for one year. (or ... a year.)",
        "x": 18.505366336808528
      },
      {
        "width": 50.92562193511635,
        "height": 1.7578690174594902,
        "y": 58.65420607318249,
        "text": "Wait here for one minute, and I’ll be with you. (or ... a minute ...)",
        "x": 19.910798889606397
      },
      {
        "width": 65.21095768097909,
        "height": 1.778896009887343,
        "y": 60.341907444171696,
        "text": "Using one gives a little more emphasis to the length of time, quantity, amount, etc.:",
        "x": 13.672585193119716
      },
      {
        "width": 73.45557264102402,
        "height": 1.8437195934217998,
        "y": 61.993725755676174,
        "text": "• He weighs one hundred and twenty kilos! Would you believe it! (using one emphasises the",
        "x": 16.69346357221455
      },
      {
        "width": 20.72434579172442,
        "height": 1.4684320999278744,
        "y": 63.953488374521136,
        "text": "weight more than using a)",
        "x": 19.71830999256727
      },
      {
        "width": 77.47663272324428,
        "height": 1.8053759659065083,
        "y": 66.09292523602596,
        "text": "However, we use one rather than a / an if we want to emphasise that we are talking about only one",
        "x": 13.274056833813836
      },
      {
        "width": 31.790743591964883,
        "height": 1.3270306425344436,
        "y": 68.16860465798091,
        "text": "thing or person rather than two or more:",
        "x": 13.480885732886428
      },
      {
        "width": 28.60518834924185,
        "height": 1.6554224733931755,
        "y": 69.60904754089157,
        "text": "Do you want one sandwich or two?",
        "x": 19.505080508666886
      },
      {
        "width": 26.358149128575477,
        "height": 1.621111750487103,
        "y": 71.36627911388996,
        "text": "Are you staying only one night?",
        "x": 18.511066277738102
      },
      {
        "width": 41.664500903057785,
        "height": 1.7901713818051501,
        "y": 72.93848775350047,
        "text": "• I just took one look at her and she started crying.",
        "x": 16.69343187985178
      },
      {
        "width": 48.71814276582451,
        "height": 1.8365674985484137,
        "y": 75.23055336081856,
        "text": "We use one, not a / an, in the pattern one ... other / another:",
        "x": 13.66991855771904
      },
      {
        "width": 30.60766240601899,
        "height": 1.695537382138801,
        "y": 77.0644189037307,
        "text": "• Close one eye, and then the other.",
        "x": 17.088225296238253
      },
      {
        "width": 35.83858859154486,
        "height": 1.7929913347838111,
        "y": 78.67278230612501,
        "text": "Bees carry pollen from one plant to another.",
        "x": 19.505073798698263
      },
      {
        "width": 45.48967833160072,
        "height": 1.638609315444839,
        "y": 81.14450488815704,
        "text": "We also use one in phrases such as one day, one evening,",
        "x": 13.873376934548997
      },
      {
        "width": 45.69056521179855,
        "height": 1.8108712019675233,
        "y": 82.8170896258734,
        "text": "one spring, etc. to mean a particular, but unspecified, day,",
        "x": 13.672194466547216
      },
      {
        "width": 15.895371795982443,
        "height": 1.1774524685020715,
        "y": 84.86905914563553,
        "text": "evening, spring, etc.:",
        "x": 13.883300020519846
      },
      {
        "width": 24.94969726890646,
        "height": 1.3213915228265538,
        "y": 86.32395730487167,
        "text": "Hope to see you again one day.",
        "x": 20.120724815946136
      },
      {
        "width": 42.87656968639743,
        "height": 1.7618164521299717,
        "y": 87.7642157291503,
        "text": "One evening, while he was working late at the office ...",
        "x": 20.108806759599833
      },
      {
        "width": 2.816901412061465,
        "height": 1.3081395198255907,
        "y": 97.23837209510174,
        "text": "88",
        "x": 4.627766587731844
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "unit": 45,
    "page": 90,
    "width": 1482,
    "height": 2062,
    "title": "A / an, the and zero article 1",
    "lines": [
      {
        "width": 6.262626081664875,
        "text": "Unit",
        "height": 2.034883656395392,
        "y": 1.8895349111433868,
        "x": 2.626262704718309
      },
      {
        "width": 5.656565410083767,
        "text": "45",
        "height": 2.7616278854651233,
        "y": 4.360465111692502,
        "x": 2.6262627562375784
      },
      {
        "width": 43.63636423540823,
        "text": "A / an, the and zero article 1",
        "height": 2.769099752609294,
        "y": 4.941860475220761,
        "x": 13.535353225825519
      },
      {
        "width": 32.52525175148659,
        "text": "We usually use the when we talk about -",
        "height": 1.6089875991776914,
        "y": 8.866279112590592,
        "x": 13.333333692587072
      },
      {
        "width": 13.939393901953645,
        "text": "Reminder → 11-19",
        "height": 1.1726591681879062,
        "y": 9.011627917940379,
        "x": 78.18181819043733
      },
      {
        "width": 61.818181294017805,
        "text": "☆ things which are unique; that is, there is only one of them (or one set of them):",
        "height": 1.4651896072520931,
        "y": 10.610465119265166,
        "x": 13.333333585247434
      },
      {
        "width": 55.55555418274503,
        "text": "the world the sky the atmosphere the sun the ground",
        "height": 1.6122300918534727,
        "y": 12.209302370418474,
        "x": 19.393940071863216
      },
      {
        "width": 38.787878862759364,
        "text": "the climate the horizon the human race",
        "height": 1.1774524685020715,
        "y": 13.953488383509127,
        "x": 19.7979797474082
      },
      {
        "width": 16.40228395037323,
        "text": "the environment",
        "height": 1.3508615392024526,
        "y": 13.908306066533328,
        "x": 58.971117685968636
      },
      {
        "width": 29.126724057834636,
        "text": "the travel industry the Internet",
        "height": 1.6866749634913858,
        "y": 15.468466006341163,
        "x": 19.778008291920855
      },
      {
        "width": 34.57246643972461,
        "text": "* general geographical areas with the as in:",
        "height": 1.8042611567056,
        "y": 17.57595467854296,
        "x": 13.317860613099054
      },
      {
        "width": 12.121211372406377,
        "text": "• the beach",
        "height": 1.182668678513099,
        "y": 19.331395346133707,
        "x": 16.767677000665504
      },
      {
        "width": 51.515150391942896,
        "text": "the town the sea(side) the land the country(side)",
        "height": 1.4736483099388797,
        "y": 19.331395351606883,
        "x": 28.686869244343654
      },
      {
        "width": 65.85858508481992,
        "text": "(where 'the country' or 'the countryside' means 'the area where there are no towns')",
        "height": 1.7660376866041827,
        "y": 20.78488373999997,
        "x": 19.797979745468837
      },
      {
        "width": 32.525251751486586,
        "text": "the past the present the future",
        "height": 1.3318238965986273,
        "y": 23.110465123308842,
        "x": 18.585858961561048
      },
      {
        "width": 76.5752918485366,
        "text": "Note, however, that some nouns like this can be used with zero article (i.e. no article) to refer to a",
        "height": 1.5476847018696005,
        "y": 25.374681824066425,
        "x": 13.530840343215061
      },
      {
        "width": 15.15151524511587,
        "text": "concept in general:",
        "height": 1.3301321653112597,
        "y": 27.303588755970342,
        "x": 13.53535348438102
      },
      {
        "width": 75.76950423308872,
        "text": "• Climate is one of the many factors involved in changing farming methods. (or The climate ...)",
        "height": 1.7621656393796647,
        "y": 28.742612978988635,
        "x": 16.762258290233227
      },
      {
        "width": 47.086930371489125,
        "text": "These flowers grow best in sandy soil and sun. (= sunshine)",
        "height": 1.7441546072899827,
        "y": 30.483694287665553,
        "x": 18.98428701479942
      },
      {
        "width": 74.5549458080297,
        "text": "• In autumn the temperature difference between land and sea decreases. (or ... the land and",
        "height": 1.6475617365277473,
        "y": 32.11285362770062,
        "x": 16.762993229998283
      },
      {
        "width": 9.29292892476647,
        "text": "the sea ...)",
        "height": 1.3236471799596972,
        "y": 33.9961202529182,
        "x": 19.595959770164466
      },
      {
        "width": 62.82828430093412,
        "text": "If we want to describe a particular instance of these we can use a / an. Compare:",
        "height": 1.3213915228265538,
        "y": 36.323957306560374,
        "x": 13.53535278983279
      },
      {
        "width": 37.77777585584303,
        "text": "• I could see the plane high up in the sky. and",
        "height": 1.4650485911031685,
        "y": 38.06983512620749,
        "x": 16.565657516632125
      },
      {
        "width": 38.585857437689775,
        "text": "• When I woke up there was a bright blue sky.",
        "height": 1.6088466292787373,
        "y": 39.67022309247956,
        "x": 16.76767732960136
      },
      {
        "width": 34.74747507195723,
        "text": "• What are your plans for the future? and",
        "height": 1.4618060984273984,
        "y": 41.41610087466505,
        "x": 16.767676595393585
      },
      {
        "width": 57.17171734643851,
        "text": "• She dreamt of a future where she could spend more time painting.",
        "height": 1.605604136602945,
        "y": 43.0164888411813,
        "x": 16.767676669839588
      },
      {
        "width": 1.6161616192816406,
        "text": "B",
        "height": 1.162790674011649,
        "y": 46.511627909118204,
        "x": 9.09090907924807
      },
      {
        "width": 79.60514784181005,
        "text": "We can use the when we make generalisations about classes of things using singular countable nouns.",
        "height": 1.60589985889098,
        "y": 46.137105323032856,
        "x": 13.73198155063505
      },
      {
        "width": 58.18181623492325,
        "text": "(See also Unit 47A.) Compare the use of the and a / an in these sentences:",
        "height": 1.310113237160826,
        "y": 47.96314256897922,
        "x": 13.53535449624062
      },
      {
        "width": 72.7412956124536,
        "text": "• The computer has revolutionised publishing. (this refers to computers in general) but not",
        "height": 1.7272392369149125,
        "y": 49.43322823582058,
        "x": 17.165286569611098
      },
      {
        "width": 68.09667672222926,
        "text": "A computer has revolutionised publishing. (computers in general have done this, not an",
        "height": 1.9202976985306042,
        "y": 51.101222893800944,
        "x": 19.79122360822607
      },
      {
        "width": 16.609689195146444,
        "text": "individual computer)",
        "height": 1.7251903633835441,
        "y": 52.8975645616842,
        "x": 19.77955786700657
      },
      {
        "width": 41.818183765076746,
        "text": "• The computer is an important research tool. and",
        "height": 1.4594094713952899,
        "y": 54.65116279356991,
        "x": 16.767675784128294
      },
      {
        "width": 70.70707045746879,
        "text": "A computer is an important research tool. (this statement is true of both the general class",
        "height": 1.4609602327837146,
        "y": 56.25000000218853,
        "x": 19.797979947311784
      },
      {
        "width": 19.0250535725582,
        "text": "and the individual item)",
        "height": 1.5350797821548134,
        "y": 57.92075928873721,
        "x": 19.78431676404786
      },
      {
        "width": 79.00519943752109,
        "text": "As an alternative to the + singular countable noun we can use a plural countable noun to talk about",
        "height": 1.6555732482850916,
        "y": 59.49155080081127,
        "x": 13.729718539683955
      },
      {
        "width": 13.233607983299592,
        "text": "a class of things:",
        "height": 1.7867623892487194,
        "y": 61.214595498167924,
        "x": 13.489520574677579
      },
      {
        "width": 37.37373712413547,
        "text": "• Computers are an important research tool.",
        "height": 1.3220964185712836,
        "y": 63.081395355969875,
        "x": 16.76767688335621
      },
      {
        "width": 74.54545694163292,
        "text": "Note that if the is used with plural and uncountable nouns we refer to a specific thing or group:",
        "height": 1.6153316146302887,
        "y": 65.4069767890217,
        "x": 13.535352328832564
      },
      {
        "width": 45.45454470573971,
        "text": "• The computers have arrived. Where shall I put them?",
        "height": 1.6168824685186545,
        "y": 67.00581397867728,
        "x": 16.767677437534175
      },
      {
        "width": 60.40403955539389,
        "text": "• The music was wonderful. I could have listened to the orchestra all night.",
        "height": 1.4730843840931152,
        "y": 68.75000000229502,
        "x": 16.969697410725743
      },
      {
        "width": 79.59595550248821,
        "text": "When we define something or say what is typical of a particular class of people or things, we generally",
        "height": 1.620970780588149,
        "y": 71.2209302774967,
        "x": 13.53535557326947
      },
      {
        "width": 20.808081170003582,
        "text": "use a / an rather than the:",
        "height": 1.0408442651728356,
        "y": 73.1104651317159,
        "x": 13.737373548248522
      },
      {
        "width": 46.66666501929402,
        "text": "• A corkscrew is a gadget for getting corks out of bottles.",
        "height": 1.4534883656395436,
        "y": 74.56395349093211,
        "x": 17.171717994569462
      },
      {
        "width": 54.94949402596786,
        "text": "• A garden is there to give you pleasure, not to be a constant worry.",
        "height": 1.4764678466678505,
        "y": 76.2851600567843,
        "x": 16.96969742028317
      },
      {
        "width": 79.60613626539303,
        "text": "Some nouns can be used uncountably when we talk about the whole substance or idea, but countably",
        "height": 1.5787956208193066,
        "y": 79.31869897330245,
        "x": 13.732002297432174
      },
      {
        "width": 79.79798104598939,
        "text": "when we talk about an instance or more than one instance of it. When these nouns are used countably",
        "height": 1.3264667166886568,
        "y": 81.08632397312635,
        "x": 13.737373112909815
      },
      {
        "width": 32.95517276655807,
        "text": "we can use a / an (and plurals). Compare:",
        "height": 1.7752487375017,
        "y": 82.73467833315522,
        "x": 13.522735720136552
      },
      {
        "width": 35.17786764744643,
        "text": "Would you like a coffee? (= a cup of coffee)",
        "height": 1.6417533881911694,
        "y": 84.31125379780866,
        "x": 45.64588228845259
      },
      {
        "width": 21.81818211770411,
        "text": "I don't drink coffee. and",
        "height": 1.3230832541139215,
        "y": 84.5780795281826,
        "x": 19.191919036501474
      },
      {
        "width": 16.60703486598294,
        "text": "He shook with fear.",
        "height": 1.5966787255006887,
        "y": 86.06476080803837,
        "x": 19.98038205663965
      },
      {
        "width": 5.719436872021549,
        "text": "and",
        "height": 1.7206613816299288,
        "y": 85.99862210425637,
        "x": 36.26505531496802
      },
      {
        "width": 22.872788896444835,
        "text": "• He has a fear of heights.",
        "height": 1.807184709609999,
        "y": 85.87598171673943,
        "x": 42.60388253840592
      },
      {
        "width": 79.1992269868632,
        "text": "There are many other nouns like this, including conversation, grammar, importance, iron, pleasure,",
        "height": 1.6401037443736444,
        "y": 88.35717085892098,
        "x": 13.934540129399709
      },
      {
        "width": 78.38383518893389,
        "text": "shampoo, sound. Some of these nouns (e.g. grammar, iron) have different meanings when they are",
        "height": 1.753772565395817,
        "y": 90.10669250933515,
        "x": 13.53535513609449
      },
      {
        "width": 26.464646065283404,
        "text": "used countably and uncountably.",
        "height": 1.4612421725816116,
        "y": 91.9980601491063,
        "x": 13.73737392751028
      },
      {
        "width": 2.8282827050418824,
        "text": "90",
        "height": 1.1627906740116378,
        "y": 96.94767442559109,
        "x": 4.444444495963908
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "unit": 46,
    "page": 92,
    "width": 1484,
    "height": 2066,
    "title": "A / an, the and zero article 2",
    "lines": [
      {
        "width": 6.166386154462705,
        "height": 2.003311533895613,
        "y": 1.9343182657119096,
        "text": "Unit",
        "x": 2.582803948516393
      },
      {
        "width": 5.870445333722467,
        "height": 2.7616279284467082,
        "y": 4.360465098968779,
        "text": "46",
        "x": 2.631578942450508
      },
      {
        "width": 44.159976105805676,
        "height": 2.969892304264443,
        "y": 4.774757022790455,
        "text": "A / an, the and zero article 2",
        "x": 13.348433200222306
      },
      {
        "width": 45.35641734490819,
        "height": 1.5891707532057375,
        "y": 8.858025969751749,
        "text": "We use a / an to say what a person's job is, was, or will be:",
        "x": 13.556043403641244
      },
      {
        "width": 13.967611719013217,
        "height": 1.1715144409445544,
        "y": 9.00290417464733,
        "text": "Reminder → 11- 19",
        "x": 78.34008077004805
      },
      {
        "width": 39.878540861638726,
        "height": 1.4637599032938486,
        "y": 10.600193587888151,
        "text": "• She was a company director when she retired.",
        "x": 16.801620248004486
      },
      {
        "width": 45.14170027164758,
        "height": 1.610656490861384,
        "y": 12.197483088529971,
        "text": "Against her parents' wishes, she wants to be a journalist.",
        "x": 19.230769292020486
      },
      {
        "width": 73.68420706283693,
        "height": 1.6123449467735584,
        "y": 13.939980679423202,
        "text": "However, when we give a person's job title, or their unique position, we use the or zero article",
        "x": 13.3603256109326
      },
      {
        "width": 28.5425109040705,
        "height": 1.468684574064416,
        "y": 15.682478218815543,
        "text": "(i.e. no article), not a / an. Compare:",
        "x": 13.360323485934671
      },
      {
        "width": 45.951415522079266,
        "height": 1.6155812539528025,
        "y": 17.279767627941702,
        "text": "• She's been appointed (the) head of the company. and",
        "x": 16.80162016548571
      },
      {
        "width": 70.86443219866072,
        "height": 1.741850595391159,
        "y": 18.778461856168228,
        "text": "I'm a production manager at Fino. (= there may be more than one production manager)",
        "x": 18.21331850659485
      },
      {
        "width": 67.62994318959527,
        "height": 1.8231607014304263,
        "y": 21.248585785897056,
        "text": "After the position of, the post of, or the role of we use zero article before a job title:",
        "x": 13.351529186949707
      },
      {
        "width": 51.214574932088105,
        "height": 1.475860580931787,
        "y": 23.08809291036893,
        "text": "• Dr Simons has taken on the position of Head of Department.",
        "x": 16.801619406425583
      },
      {
        "width": 79.96732398184805,
        "height": 1.7117848354756826,
        "y": 26.213461830938723,
        "text": "We usually use zero article (i.e. no article) before the name of an individual person or place. However,",
        "x": 13.355402171640678
      },
      {
        "width": 1.4170040017511014,
        "height": 1.1627907212913735,
        "y": 26.7441860263975,
        "text": "B",
        "x": 9.109311754185176
      },
      {
        "width": 10.202488038096465,
        "height": 1.3463577019395156,
        "y": 28.108789314104875,
        "text": "we use the -",
        "x": 13.518500139632314
      },
      {
        "width": 62.15821957652459,
        "height": 1.6342449280553284,
        "y": 29.60963780863771,
        "text": "* when there are two people with the same name to specify which one we mean:",
        "x": 13.557652002096304
      },
      {
        "width": 44.33198502121589,
        "height": 1.3248835043893292,
        "y": 31.39534882782604,
        "text": "• That's not the Stephen Fraser I went to school with.",
        "x": 17.206477165216228
      },
      {
        "width": 69.8627482206031,
        "height": 2.0595515455188673,
        "y": 32.71490010057778,
        "text": "but compare 'There was a Stephen Fraser in my class.' (= a person named Stephen Fraser)",
        "x": 13.348855463354909
      },
      {
        "width": 77.55117082210242,
        "height": 1.779996644838966,
        "y": 34.93848666252693,
        "text": "☆ when we want to emphasise that the person we are referring to is the most famous person with that",
        "x": 13.75547683387911
      },
      {
        "width": 43.94794885681647,
        "height": 1.6213979287161395,
        "y": 36.75657429275348,
        "text": "name. Used this way, the is stressed and pronounced /ðiː/:",
        "x": 16.79115816569492
      },
      {
        "width": 45.369500419842915,
        "height": 1.7107789075617053,
        "y": 38.32277059096756,
        "text": "• Do they mean the Neil Armstrong, or someone else?",
        "x": 16.791804750386678
      },
      {
        "width": 61.75277175286388,
        "height": 1.6800990293933116,
        "y": 40.39499842031766,
        "text": "* with an adjective to describe a person, or another noun which tells us their job:",
        "x": 13.75938379768464
      },
      {
        "width": 23.481781334889863,
        "height": 1.3143305856976095,
        "y": 42.29651161971819,
        "text": "• the late Michael Jackson",
        "x": 17.00404859233218
      },
      {
        "width": 66.82428323997641,
        "height": 1.9084701464229359,
        "y": 43.55500547842608,
        "text": "• (the) artist Joseph Turner ('the' is sometimes left out, particularly in journalism)",
        "x": 16.79119958976962
      },
      {
        "width": 33.40080857598235,
        "height": 1.6012291478972207,
        "y": 45.930232595380716,
        "text": "* when we talk about a family as a whole:",
        "x": 13.562753403051339
      },
      {
        "width": 34.21052588285461,
        "height": 1.5995407843058973,
        "y": 47.674418558903554,
        "text": "• The Robinsons are away this weekend.",
        "x": 16.801619643057588
      },
      {
        "width": 75.32912920106132,
        "height": 1.9342974563997473,
        "y": 50.471200164829376,
        "text": "Note that a / an, or sometimes zero article, is used with a name when referring to the particular",
        "x": 13.954692678219766
      },
      {
        "width": 31.39846061439206,
        "height": 1.5097870138930936,
        "y": 52.461943028371415,
        "text": "excellent qualities of the person named:",
        "x": 13.955277568249247
      },
      {
        "width": 50.4386716775817,
        "height": 2.04839180192089,
        "y": 53.87739300737488,
        "text": "• Majid plays tennis well, but he'll never be (a) Roger Federer.",
        "x": 17.190179319565914
      },
      {
        "width": 72.07660520815786,
        "height": 1.5607883715560322,
        "y": 56.324951037110914,
        "text": "We also use a / an when we refer to an individual example of a product made by a particular",
        "x": 13.961210177286867
      },
      {
        "width": 76.55419198007918,
        "height": 2.190110390322475,
        "y": 57.82796368695783,
        "text": "manufacturer (e.g. I’ve just bought a Mercedes) or a work by a particular artist (e.g. Do you think it",
        "x": 13.748005813128286
      },
      {
        "width": 30.402326969444914,
        "height": 1.8795037431153738,
        "y": 59.75227795515073,
        "text": "could be a Van Gogh / a Rembrandt?).",
        "x": 13.74090269669333
      },
      {
        "width": 70.67542885834315,
        "height": 1.949320181064662,
        "y": 62.004778236474664,
        "text": "You can use a / an before a person's name if you don't know the person yourself. Compare:",
        "x": 13.956163933174256
      },
      {
        "width": 35.65647094397533,
        "height": 1.7335563061428916,
        "y": 63.945572780998496,
        "text": "Dr Lee is here for you. (= I know Dr Lee) and",
        "x": 19.016462882330423
      },
      {
        "width": 73.71397609659283,
        "height": 2.0887867871235533,
        "y": 65.30041026937519,
        "text": "There's a Dr Amy Lee on the phone. (= I haven't heard of her before) Do you want to talk to her?",
        "x": 19.82597402296719
      },
      {
        "width": 74.33113036451314,
        "height": 2.2224501972623156,
        "y": 68.39678943152151,
        "text": "In stories and jokes in conversation, this is commonly used instead of a / an to introduce a new",
        "x": 13.94980575257662
      },
      {
        "width": 73.12376120019795,
        "height": 2.2496281611838698,
        "y": 70.09657311530792,
        "text": "person or thing. Using this highlights the person or thing as the topic of what is to come next:",
        "x": 13.944199018439516
      },
      {
        "width": 57.514941274637806,
        "height": 2.063241609645372,
        "y": 71.89787423883416,
        "text": "As I was walking along, this spider (= a spider) landed on my head, and ...",
        "x": 20.22989797042775
      },
      {
        "width": 42.73297086237575,
        "height": 1.6180503749201103,
        "y": 73.77809075969223,
        "text": "This man (= a man) goes into a chemist and he says ...",
        "x": 20.63605674789205
      },
      {
        "width": 71.49229640909283,
        "height": 2.132652112844491,
        "y": 76.77495679745171,
        "text": "We use the before a superlative adjective (the biggest, the most expensive, etc.) when the",
        "x": 14.153704433223641
      },
      {
        "width": 1.214574932088107,
        "height": 1.1627906289705336,
        "y": 77.4709302523752,
        "text": "E",
        "x": 10.121457463105745
      },
      {
        "width": 48.20657406213148,
        "height": 1.7124283117569417,
        "y": 78.69848581585308,
        "text": "superlative adjective is followed by a noun or defining phrase:",
        "x": 14.156441331779732
      },
      {
        "width": 44.361425024479864,
        "height": 1.9947068619704966,
        "y": 80.27710843366073,
        "text": "• He is the finest young player around at the moment.",
        "x": 17.597995311812685
      },
      {
        "width": 74.7375735054119,
        "height": 2.327370620535507,
        "y": 82.40894375837317,
        "text": "However, we can often leave out the, particularly in an informal style, when there is no noun or",
        "x": 14.147997177123644
      },
      {
        "width": 44.14608279328463,
        "height": 1.5184455088701365,
        "y": 84.56054465202246,
        "text": "defining phrase after the superlative adjective. Compare:",
        "x": 14.364204124304758
      },
      {
        "width": 37.089423413546584,
        "height": 1.8863443483572384,
        "y": 86.03434513616055,
        "text": "• A: Why did you decide to stay in this hotel?",
        "x": 17.3904397324426
      },
      {
        "width": 48.61972531218414,
        "height": 1.9724443367351574,
        "y": 87.59308469902587,
        "text": "B: It was (the) cheapest. and It was the cheapest I could find.",
        "x": 20.626706468794612
      },
      {
        "width": 2.631578933839207,
        "height": 1.3081394575918504,
        "y": 96.94767444089885,
        "text": "92",
        "x": 5.263157873667441
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "unit": 47,
    "page": 94,
    "width": 1484,
    "height": 2065,
    "title": "A / an, the and zero article 3",
    "lines": [
      {
        "width": 6.275303473048455,
        "text": "Unit",
        "height": 1.889534956718808,
        "y": 1.8895348431143044,
        "x": 2.024291571432119
      },
      {
        "width": 5.870445333722467,
        "text": "47",
        "height": 2.906976757068025,
        "y": 4.21511626630926,
        "x": 2.226720642855366
      },
      {
        "width": 44.1295531239471,
        "text": "A / an, the and zero article 3",
        "height": 2.9116200339067144,
        "y": 4.791868343896899,
        "x": 12.955466343647668
      },
      {
        "width": 57.51518804750675,
        "text": "With plural and uncountable nouns, zero article (i.e. no article) is used to",
        "height": 1.9238788645357552,
        "y": 8.574351180355489,
        "x": 12.942118565519495
      },
      {
        "width": 1.6194331999416307,
        "text": "A",
        "height": 1.453488378534018,
        "y": 9.011627889221362,
        "x": 8.299595128774124
      },
      {
        "width": 14.170040531621153,
        "text": "Reminder → 11-19",
        "height": 1.1713737439786098,
        "y": 8.857696034403972,
        "x": 77.73279348940122
      },
      {
        "width": 60.750150037904305,
        "text": "talk generally, without definite people or things in mind. The is used when we",
        "height": 1.9515247104936462,
        "y": 10.279052175649362,
        "x": 12.74224727615387
      },
      {
        "width": 60.93117438879296,
        "text": "assume the listener or reader will understand who or what we are referring to,",
        "height": 1.4653076622400785,
        "y": 12.197483038340229,
        "x": 12.753036278315012
      },
      {
        "width": 61.55205081415305,
        "text": "or when other words in the noun phrase make the reference specific. Compare:",
        "height": 1.5834472301737956,
        "y": 13.77111111184195,
        "x": 12.948855714560366
      },
      {
        "width": 59.735263711358655,
        "text": "• The government has promised not to tax books. (= books generally) and",
        "height": 1.7864126665202207,
        "y": 15.450077698074882,
        "x": 16.187283009099808
      },
      {
        "width": 41.29554769099562,
        "text": "The books have arrived. (= the books you ordered)",
        "height": 1.470232333010646,
        "y": 17.27976766976399,
        "x": 17.813764608465075
      },
      {
        "width": 54.479351197934214,
        "text": "• Music played an important part in his life. (= music generally) and",
        "height": 1.8784405762782286,
        "y": 18.744482073728697,
        "x": 16.385997802777123
      },
      {
        "width": 65.39742606026786,
        "text": "• I thought the music used in the film was the best part. (= that particular music)",
        "height": 1.7967829745829,
        "y": 20.465446077781245,
        "x": 16.18829361936679
      },
      {
        "width": 1.6194331999416292,
        "text": "B",
        "height": 1.3081395499126902,
        "y": 24.127906958328538,
        "x": 8.502024280595986
      },
      {
        "width": 78.34007900680172,
        "text": "We often use zero article with the names of holidays, special times of the year, months, and days of",
        "height": 1.645692158760892,
        "y": 23.668925429101616,
        "x": 12.955466581703732
      },
      {
        "width": 54.88036122283525,
        "text": "the week including Easter, Ramadan, New Year's Day. But compare:",
        "height": 1.9081699190389045,
        "y": 25.348856389368557,
        "x": 12.743399834914129
      },
      {
        "width": 35.057499723614384,
        "text": "I’ll see you on Saturday. (= next Saturday)",
        "height": 2.026408916521394,
        "y": 27.100495136600177,
        "x": 17.799191505094303
      },
      {
        "width": 30.97166076824671,
        "text": "We met on Saturday. (= last Saturday)",
        "height": 1.6176918007628105,
        "y": 28.924418558601083,
        "x": 19.230768804330868
      },
      {
        "width": 72.69101207147068,
        "text": "They came on a Saturday as far as I can remember. (we are only interested in the day of the",
        "height": 1.9091843404705156,
        "y": 30.235383178750965,
        "x": 18.413650657999963
      },
      {
        "width": 29.554655995330403,
        "text": "week, not which particular Saturday)",
        "height": 1.469247408088603,
        "y": 32.267441856454695,
        "x": 19.230769163486006
      },
      {
        "width": 72.4964152127906,
        "text": "• They came on the Saturday after our party. (a particular Saturday, specifying which one)",
        "height": 2.073197766402801,
        "y": 33.603495745499146,
        "x": 16.387135976298364
      },
      {
        "width": 75.74326342970856,
        "text": "With winter, summer, spring, autumn, and New Year (meaning the holiday period), we can use",
        "height": 2.2210130386869587,
        "y": 35.95116822659532,
        "x": 13.141536277365192
      },
      {
        "width": 20.274554558520048,
        "text": "either zero article or the:",
        "height": 1.3641063841591805,
        "y": 38.058675254440466,
        "x": 13.343372009698177
      },
      {
        "width": 55.27828658687458,
        "text": "• In (the) summer I try to spend as much time as I can in the garden.",
        "height": 1.7296908324131777,
        "y": 39.49641419733831,
        "x": 16.995392291489523
      },
      {
        "width": 73.50703236870366,
        "text": "We use the when it is understood or we go on to specify which summer, spring, etc. we mean:",
        "height": 1.9163929365957566,
        "y": 41.12178167977121,
        "x": 13.145975952830685
      },
      {
        "width": 39.878540861638726,
        "text": "• I'd like to go skiing in the autumn. (= this year)",
        "height": 1.6040433641786533,
        "y": 43.02325576822186,
        "x": 16.599191103316063
      },
      {
        "width": 34.61538556451104,
        "text": "• I first went skiing in the spring of 2002.",
        "height": 1.6023549082664568,
        "y": 44.76744181460206,
        "x": 16.396760654814567
      },
      {
        "width": 51.8367880438216,
        "text": "We say 'in the New Year' to mean near the beginning of next year:",
        "height": 1.733092393902813,
        "y": 46.25278094165508,
        "x": 13.149641728377482
      },
      {
        "width": 29.78523233830126,
        "text": "I'll see you again in the New Year.",
        "height": 1.7149169124222818,
        "y": 47.96886268327225,
        "x": 17.190949583317614
      },
      {
        "width": 79.17569306982817,
        "text": "When we want to describe the features of a particular holiday, season, or other period of time and say",
        "height": 1.9248284767350299,
        "y": 50.192520435261635,
        "x": 13.549706464560748
      },
      {
        "width": 79.58433248926045,
        "text": "that it was somehow special when compared with others, we can use It / That was ... + a / an + noun",
        "height": 2.056430362431838,
        "y": 51.818447609844185,
        "x": 13.346743799629031
      },
      {
        "width": 24.696356266977972,
        "text": "+ modifying phrase. Compare:",
        "height": 1.4574281243825538,
        "y": 54.06582769170672,
        "x": 13.360323879019322
      },
      {
        "width": 73.52011955651955,
        "text": "• That was a winter I'll never forget. (= compared to other winters it was unforgettable) and",
        "height": 2.187047000083664,
        "y": 55.13681440416622,
        "x": 16.582822388753453
      },
      {
        "width": 67.64752164362578,
        "text": "• That was the winter we went to Norway. (= a statement about a particular winter)",
        "height": 2.124182598634705,
        "y": 56.82474064412892,
        "x": 16.58250998107799
      },
      {
        "width": 70.89318123789168,
        "text": "We use zero article with times of the day and night such as midnight, midday, and noon:",
        "height": 2.3895793593518344,
        "y": 60.04424173709906,
        "x": 13.341002844169706
      },
      {
        "width": 33.60323841681057,
        "text": "If possible, I’d like it finished by midday.",
        "height": 1.610656490861384,
        "y": 62.19748308826777,
        "x": 18.01619455123673
      },
      {
        "width": 35.25111771658103,
        "text": "• Midnight couldn't come quickly enough.",
        "height": 1.8682601721912273,
        "y": 63.744698301045254,
        "x": 16.988824065029316
      },
      {
        "width": 40.31313667400186,
        "text": "But note that we can say either the dawn or dawn:",
        "height": 1.680987248231458,
        "y": 65.46425903469363,
        "x": 13.75169702741399
      },
      {
        "width": 41.3343280473488,
        "text": "• He got back into bed and waited for (the) dawn.",
        "height": 1.940502524952914,
        "y": 67.02434992097638,
        "x": 16.984095957921305
      },
      {
        "width": 75.34762071470686,
        "text": "We use the + morning / afternoon / evening for a day which is understood or already specified:",
        "height": 2.347307583715652,
        "y": 69.15506841271352,
        "x": 13.744060714183634
      },
      {
        "width": 56.301538513677144,
        "text": "• I enjoyed the morning, but in the afternoon the course was boring.",
        "height": 1.9703526233772806,
        "y": 71.0439537215,
        "x": 16.790232324399312
      },
      {
        "width": 10.757314676865734,
        "text": "But compare:",
        "height": 1.2378585534774333,
        "y": 73.31618622788623,
        "x": 13.95036231180375
      },
      {
        "width": 72.70564570259856,
        "text": "• Morning is the time I work best. (= mornings in general; The morning ... is also possible)",
        "height": 2.1937548479521563,
        "y": 74.19460722528693,
        "x": 16.987268086718764
      },
      {
        "width": 69.47254273448029,
        "text": "I'll be there by (the) morning / evening. (but ... by the afternoon, not ... by afternoon)",
        "height": 2.224410261096932,
        "y": 75.89160954514718,
        "x": 19.621598965738478
      },
      {
        "width": 56.50778305177098,
        "text": "I waited all morning. (more usual than all the morning / afternoon, etc.)",
        "height": 1.925212162161849,
        "y": 77.7554693859819,
        "x": 19.826600227020407
      },
      {
        "width": 65.43113523416442,
        "text": "‘You look upset.’ ‘Yes, I’ve had a terrible morning.’ (= compared to other mornings)",
        "height": 2.458424397382708,
        "y": 79.07205309223816,
        "x": 19.62000548875325
      },
      {
        "width": 74.52881188405492,
        "text": "We often use by + zero article to talk about means of transport and communication. Compare:",
        "height": 2.0905514077318554,
        "y": 82.46185590096266,
        "x": 14.152664434903613
      },
      {
        "width": 1.8218622696046238,
        "text": "D",
        "height": 1.1627907212913735,
        "y": 83.43023253802542,
        "x": 9.311740919853557
      },
      {
        "width": 35.4530108264193,
        "text": "and • I generally take the bus to work.",
        "height": 1.6698206728910314,
        "y": 84.22655168596408,
        "x": 43.9125619020772
      },
      {
        "width": 26.376688255454013,
        "text": "I generally go by bus to work.",
        "height": 1.9880488673576613,
        "y": 84.42676136784316,
        "x": 17.78427974901967
      },
      {
        "width": 44.38935971324335,
        "text": "Also: go / travel by car / taxi / bus / plane / train / air /",
        "height": 2.1038098810718497,
        "y": 86.7685302665966,
        "x": 14.955066579642462
      },
      {
        "width": 42.754057604026286,
        "text": "sea; contact / communicate by post / email / phone",
        "height": 1.8339587319624262,
        "y": 88.58905428271393,
        "x": 15.162401891392067
      },
      {
        "width": 2.834008003502201,
        "text": "94",
        "height": 1.3081395499126902,
        "y": 96.94767440514408,
        "x": 4.858299632772272
      }
    ]
  }
]
